<code>assert !Objects.isNull(c) => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the collection `c` is not null, then the constructed list has the same size as `c` and each element at index `i` in the new list is equal to the element at index `i` in the array representation of `c`.
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the collection `c` is not empty, then every element in the constructed `ArrayList` is equal to the corresponding element in the array obtained from `c.toArray()`. This ensures that the `ArrayList` is initialized with the same elements as the collection `c`.
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
